    "answer": {
      "state": "completed",
      "text": "Decision: Discharge home with a supported care package, which honours her stated wish. Do not discharge her home without support today. Record the disposition as \"home with support, pending carer arrangement.\" She is not cleared to leave until the carer arrangement is confirmed.\n\nJustification:\n\n**Medically ready**\n- Priya Tanaka (Ward 4, Bed 14, day 6) has been clinically stable for the last 24 hours.\n- All her blood results are back, with nothing outstanding.\n- Her discharge medications are reconciled against her home list, with no changes and no interactions.\n\n**Barrier to going home unsupported**\n- She needs a frame to mobilise.\n- She needs someone with her on stairs.\n- There is no one at her home and no carer arrangement in place.\n- Sending her home alone would leave that assistance need unmet.\n\n**Patient preference**\n- She has said several times that she wants to go back home.\n- Home with support is therefore the preferred route, rather than an alternative placement.\n\n**Outstanding actions before discharge**\n1. Arrange a carer or support package that covers help with mobility and stairs (social work and case management).\n2. Book an outpatient clinic appointment, as none is booked yet.\n\n**Gaps**\n- The evidence does not show whether her daughter or any other person could provide the support.\n- It does not show whether a home care package is available or how soon.\n- If support cannot be put in place, this disposition will need to be reviewed with the team and with the patient.",
